      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242845",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/84/84da1d2e9f5ced8e5a61c6ff33ff27ac4f476f8ab23fe5894abf3ce1296d3aac.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows a circle $C$ of radius $1$ centered at $A(3, 2)$ and the unit circle $U$ centered at the origin $O$. Prove that $C$ is similar to $U$.\n\nTo prove that $C$ is similar to $U$, we construct a sequence of similarity transformations that map $C$ onto $U$.\n\nNote that a translation of\n{{field-1}}\nand\n{{field-2}}\nmaps the circle $C$ onto the circle $U$."
