      ":question/problem": "![](images/7a/7a8ca62f0be867da767bd7349d7a9b1a568574d94697ae9dc3c5b2fa2edacb07.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows a circle $C$ of radius $3$ centered at the origin $O$ and the unit circle $U$ centered also at the origin $O$. Prove that $C$ is similar to $U$.\n\nTo prove that $C$ is similar to $U$, we construct a sequence of similarity transformations that map $C$ onto $U$.\n\nNote that a dilation of\n{{field-1}}\nand\n{{field-2}}\nmaps the circle $C$ onto the circle $U$."
